==============================================================================
ADDENDUM (verification of refutations)
==============================================================================
SCALE INVARIANCE: measS7(c*E)=measS7(E) exactly for all c (confirmed) => uniform widening is
  a MEASURE-PRESERVING SYMMETRY, not a mixing contraction. H3 (Lyapunov/cat-map decoupling) DEAD.
COMPRESSION MONOTONICITY (k=8, 5446 single-gap compressions): 2145 VIOLATIONS. Compressing a gap
  can LOWER measS7 (e.g. {0..6,10}->{0..6,9}). So consec is the global max but NOT reachable by a
  monotone compression gradient flow. H2 (consec=renorm fixed pt) is only true as 'minimal span',
  not as a hyperbolic dynamical fixed point.
THREE-GAP / STEINHAUS: breakpoint set {m/(7e): e in E} has 6/9/11 distinct gaps at k=7/8/9 (>3),
  so the classical three-distance law does NOT apply. The cover is a SUPERPOSITION of many
  rotation orbits (one per e), NOT a single CF-renormalizable orbit => no cat-map. This is the
  dynamical face of HYP-2704 (irreducibly aggregate).
SURVIVING POSITIVE RESULT: PART 0 -- exact 7-band integer-part split S_e=(e*j+floor(e*a)) mod 7,
  cover EXACTLY 7-periodic in j (a clean derivation of the HYP-2703 7-band structure).
